  "notes": "Dark Scandinavian electropop with a blunt lyric register. The drum block is authored from a texture claim rather than a pattern one: \"heavy programmed kick, distorted clap on 2&4, and long reverb tails; sparse hats. Percussion is used as a texture block that enters and leaves whole.\" So the velocity tiers are the loudest in this batch, the snare is a hard-transient clap under a large tail, `hihat.continuous` is false at `fillDensity` 0.1 with the roll vocabulary off, and the perc density bottoms out at 0 — the block genuinely leaves. The low end is a synth, not an 808: \"distorted synth sub locked to the kick, mixed loud; the low end plus the vocal is often the whole arrangement\", so no `bass808` block is authored and the bassline is a kick mirror at 0.97 with almost no passing motion. Harmony is \"4-bar minor loops with 7ths\" plus \"a sustained tonic drone\", which is the tonic family and the `vamp`-weighted rhythm. The melody block encodes \"chant-like with a repeated single-note hook and a leap into a strained top note\" as `motifPitchCount` 2 — the smallest authored in this section — with a high `riff` contour and a raised `octaveJumpProb` for the strained leap; \"countermelody is a pitched vocal sample\" is `bell_echo` first. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research says the parameters are \"largely inferred\": every drum probability, the humanize pair, the harmonic weights, the melody register and `bpm.mode` 110 (the midpoint of the stated 95—125 band) are INFERRED. ⚠ The entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the vocal-tone claim is repeated here.",
